ELEMENTARY TRANS  Fundamental Property
The general solutions of the equations
sin t=z
cos t=z
tan t=z
are respectively
4.4.10   t=Arcsin z=(-1)^k  arcsin z+k\pi
4.4.11   t=Arccos z=\pm arccos z+2k\pi
4.4.12   t=Artcan z=arctan z+k\pi   (z^2\neq-1)
where k is an arbitrary integer.
4.4.13   Interval containing principal value
y   x positive or zero
arcsin x and arctan x  0<y<\pi/2  -\pi/2<y<0
arccos x and arccot x  0<y<\pi/2  \pi/2<y<\pi
arcsec x and arcsec x  0<y<\pi/2  -\pi<y<\pi/2
arcsin x and arccot x  0<y<\pi/2  -\pi<y<\pi/2
Figure 4.5: Inverse circular functions. Functions of Negative Arguments
4.4.14   arcsin (−z)=-arcsin z
4.4.15   arccos (−z)=\pi-arccos z
4.4.16   arctan (−z)=-arctan z
4.4.17   arccsc (−z)=-arccsc z
4.4.18   arcsec (−z)=\pi-arsec z
4.4.19   arccot (−z)=\pi-arccot z
Relation to Inverse Hyperbolic Functions (see 4.6.14 to 4.6.19)
4.4.20   Arcsin z=-i Arcsinh iz
4.4.21   Arccos z=\pi i Arccosh z
4.4.22   Arctan z=-i Arctan hiz  (z^2\neq-1)